  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday night through next Thursday)\nIssued at 1131 AM CST Fri Nov 27 2026\n\nWinds will quickly diminish on Sunday morning, and will even fall \nbelow 10 mph by Sunday afternoon as a transient surface ridge builds \noverhead. Temperatures on Sunday will be noticably cooler with highs \nonly expected to reach the upper 40s to mid 50s, but clear skies \nwill continue. Flow aloft is progged to remain mostly zonal from \nMonday through midweek, which will bring a return of persistent \nsouthwesterly to westerly surface flow across West TX. Consequently, \ntemperatures will quickly recover back above normal on Monday with \nhighs in the 60s and 70s likely each day Mon-Wed. During the second \nhalf of the week, a majority of models bring a deep cutoff low \neastward from the SoCal coast into the Desert SW. This will very \nlikely bring another cooldown by Thu/Fri, but precip chances are \nstill hit or miss with low confidence in the precise evolution of \nthe system.",
